      "content": "It's understandable that unsolved dental pain is bothering you, especially when it affects your sleep. However, taking ibuprofen with omeprazole could still cause stomach issues due to their combined effects on the gastrointestinal tract. While omeprazole lowers stomach acid production and might somewhat protect your stomach lining, ibuprofen, even in a smaller dose, can still irritate it. Given the current discomfort and the inflamed state caused by your upper stomach issues, I strongly suggest avoiding ibuprofen for now. Instead, consider using a gentle dental rinse to decrease bacteria and possibly alleviate some toothache symptoms. If the pain persists in the morning, you can evaluate whether the ibuprofen truly is necessary after consulting a healthcare professional next week. In the meantime, again, maintaining a gentle oral hygiene routine could provide some solace from your dental discomfort.",
